# Issues vs git

- GitHub Issues on the owning child = open work and decisions. Close when decided, not when a PR exists.
- Git = facts that would otherwise lie. One canonical file; pointers elsewhere.
- PRs preferred for decoder, wire-contract, and plugin runtime changes. Not required. Direct push to `main` is allowed on first-party children.

## Do not

- Restate an issue verdict in parent README and child docs in the same change.
- Treat the parent as a build root.

## Do

- Edit the child that owns the fact, then bump the parent pin.
- Point to [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) and [docs/pin-bump.md](docs/pin-bump.md).
